		(property "Note" "as made: Pico A's 3.3 V clock goes straight to the chips.  For a 5 V clock (in case a donor chip does not accept 3.3 V): CUT 1-2 FIRST, then bridge 2-3; the clock then passes through a gate of U5 (inverted, about 10 ns later).  Bridging 2-3 without cutting 1-2 sets the gate against Pico A's pin"
